Instruction Fetch 

Project Overview
This project implements the Instruction Fetch (IF) stage of a processor using Verilog HDL. The design is divided into individual modules that can be tested 
independently.

**Design Modules**
    1. Mux (mux.v)
    Selects between two 32-bit inputs based on a one-bit selection signal.
    •	sel = 1: Selects a_true.
    •	sel = 0: Selects b_false.
    •	Uses a parameter to configure the data width.

    2. Instruction Memory (instrMem.v)
    Stores instruction words and returns the instruction associated with a given address.
    •	Uses a clock and reset signal.
    •	Supports read and write operations through a shared bidirectional data bus.
    •	The testbench writes dummy instruction patterns to the first 10 addresses and reads them back for verification.

    3. Incrementer (incrementer.v)
    Calculates the next program counter value by adding one to the input.
    •	Uses a clock and reset signal.
    •	Captures the incremented input on the rising edge of the clock.
    •	Resets its internal register to zero when reset is asserted.

    4. Program Counter (pc.v)
    Stores the current program counter value and updates it according to the clock and reset behavior defined by the module.


    6. Fetch Stage (fetch.v)
    Integrates the PC, instruction memory, incrementer, mux, and IF/ID latch into one module.
    The stage selects the next PC, fetches the corresponding instruction, and passes the instruction and next-PC value to the IF/ID interface.


**Testbenches**
Each individual module has a corresponding testbench where applicable.
•	mux_tb.v: Tests both mux selection paths.
•	instrMem_tb.v: Tests writing and reading instruction patterns.
•	incrementer_tb.v: Tests reset behavior and incrementing across clock cycles.

